From 91f075bdcc329ec754e10e24da3cce36c5279784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:43:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: read the swap weapon's acid resistance from its acid
 element

When the Borg records the flags of its chosen swap weapon, the acid
resistance flag was set from the weapon's electricity resistance.  A
swap weapon that resists only lightning therefore counted as acid
resistance, and one that resists acid was not counted at all.  The
preparedness check for depths 26 and deeper uses that flag, so a Borg
whose only 'acid resistance' was a lightning-resisting swap weapon
considered itself ready for those depths.

Read the acid flag from the acid element, as the swap scan earlier in
the same function and the armour swap already do.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#199.

(cherry picked from commit eddbf5b82293ea70a76fae960bc9f8debf1579c6)
---
 src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c b/src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c
index 81e8c909a..b629dbebc 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c
@@ -711,7 +711,7 @@ void borg_notice_weapon_swap(void)
         weapon_swap_immune_elec = true;
 
     /* Resistance flags */
-    if (item->el_info[ELEM_ELEC].res_level > 0)
+    if (item->el_info[ELEM_ACID].res_level > 0)
         weapon_swap_resist_acid = true;
     if (item->el_info[ELEM_ELEC].res_level > 0)
         weapon_swap_resist_elec = true;
